[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5352344630","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122511#issuecomment-5352344630","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122511","id":5352344630,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPwZMNg","user":{"login":"Synzorasize","id":60207816,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMjA3ODE2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60207816?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize","html_url":"https://github.com/Synzorasize","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-20T06:39:17Z","updated_at":"2026-08-20T06:39:17Z","body":"Tbh, idk why `_printerr` was needed to begin with instead of `ERR_PRINT(vformat(\"%s:%d - Parse Error: %s.\", res_path, lines, error_text));`. Most functions in other classes use the macro directly. Maybe to avoid repetition, but I think easy debugging should be preferred over this.\n\nI think it would be good if the `_printerr` included the line number of the code that caused it so it's easier to debug. Not sure how that can be done without hardcoding the line numbers (since they can always change), but maybe doing something with the debugger in Godot (to print the second degree of the backtrace, or in fact print the full backtrace if using the dev builds).\n\nOf course, this can be hidden on non-dev builds. I think that would need a proposal, though.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5352344630/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5355930365","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122511#issuecomment-5355930365","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122511","id":5355930365,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPz0C_Q","user":{"login":"leandro-benedet-garcia","id":291051,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTA1MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/291051?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandro-benedet-garcia","html_url":"https://github.com/leandro-benedet-garcia","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandro-benedet-garcia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandro-benedet-garcia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandro-benedet-garcia/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandro-benedet-garcia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandro-benedet-garcia/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandro-benedet-garcia/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandro-benedet-garcia/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandro-benedet-garcia/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandro-benedet-garcia/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-20T12:32:50Z","updated_at":"2026-08-20T12:32:50Z","body":"> Tbh, idk why `_printerr` was needed to begin with instead of `ERR_PRINT(vformat(\"%s:%d - Parse Error: %s.\", res_path, lines, error_text));`. Most functions in other classes use the macro directly. Maybe to avoid repetition, but I think easy debugging should be preferred over this.\n> \n> I think it would be good if the `_printerr` included the line number of the code that caused it so it's easier to debug. Not sure how that can be done without hardcoding the line numbers (since they can always change), but maybe doing something with the debugger in Godot (to print the second degree of the backtrace, or in fact print the full backtrace if using the dev builds).\n> \n> Of course, this can be hidden on non-dev builds. I think that would need a proposal, though.\n\nA easier thing to do is to make `vformat(\"%s:%d - Parse Error: %s.\", res_path, lines, error_text)` into a function and then just put the macro directly on the line and where applicable, use other `ERR_*` macros.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5355930365/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5359166191","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122511#issuecomment-5359166191","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122511","id":5359166191,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABP25i7w","user":{"login":"Synzorasize","id":60207816,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMjA3ODE2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60207816?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize","html_url":"https://github.com/Synzorasize","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-20T17:05:35Z","updated_at":"2026-08-20T17:05:35Z","body":"So you suggest something like this (in [`scene/resources/resource_format_text.cpp`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/3000096f9aa6f46db98d3a6d2a9442d58cab96ac/scene/resources/resource_format_text.cpp#L41), of course, since these three are private):\n```c++\n#define PRINTERR \\\n\t_err_print_error(FUNCTION_STR, __FILE__, __LINE__, vformat(\"%s:%d - Parse Error: %s.\", res_path, lines, error_text));\n```\nAnd then it can be used like so here:\n```c++\nerror_text = \"Unexpected end of file\"; \nPRINTERR;\nerror = ERR_FILE_CORRUPT;\n```\nI'm guessing (don't know much about the error system)? If so, then yes, that can solve the issue, hopefully. I haven't tested if that compiles though, but you can check. (Also `#undef`ing it at the end of course)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5359166191/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5359229221","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122511#issuecomment-5359229221","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122511","id":5359229221,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABP29ZJQ","user":{"login":"leandro-benedet-garcia","id":291051,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTA1MQ==","avatar_u